==== OEM easy install ====
Use the router's web interface, look for firmware upgrade page, select the *-AR5315u-squashfs-cfe.bin firmware and proceed.

==== Flashing via bootloader web ====
With this procedure you will flash the firmware using the [[docs:techref:bootloader|bootloader]] web interface (foolproof)
  - Set a **static IP** on your computer, use 192.168.1.35 (or any compatible), and connect the ethernet cable to the router.
  - Unplug the router's power cord
  - Press the button labeled as //RESET//, **don't** release it yet!
  - Plug the power cord
  - Wait 6 seconds or more until the power LED stays red fixed
  - Release the //RESET// button
  - Browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1%%'' and you should see this screen:\\ {{:media:doc:cfe63xx_web-upgrade.png?500|}}
  - Select .bin firmware
  - Press //Update Software// to start the firmware update process
  - Wait for it to reboot
  - Telnet / ssh to 192.168.1.1 and set a root password, or browse to ''%%http://192.168.1.1%%'' if LuCI is installed.



